    <!-- http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#T1548.006 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#T1548.006">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#T1548"/>
        <attack-id>T1548.006</attack-id>
        <definition>Adversaries can manipulate or abuse the Transparency, Consent, &amp; Control (TCC) service or database to execute malicious applications with elevated permissions. TCC is a Privacy &amp; Security macOS control mechanism used to determine if the running process has permission to access the data or services protected by TCC, such as screen sharing, camera, microphone, or Full Disk Access (FDA).</definition>
        <rdfs:label>TCC Manipulation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


