        <definition>Audio input devices allow a user to send audio info to a computer for processing, recording, or carrying out commands. Devices such as microphones allow users to speak to the computer in order to record a voice message or navigate software. Aside from recording, audio input devices are also used with speech recognition software.</definition>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Input_device#Voice_input_devices"/>
