    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#GoodmanAndKruskalsGamma">
        <definition>Goodman-Kruskal $\\gamma$ is a measure of rank correlation between x and y and is given by $(n_c -n_d) / (n_c + n_d)$, where $n_c$ is the number of concordant pairs of the observations and $n_d$ is the number of discordant pairs.</definition>
        <kb-article>## References
1. Wolfram Research. (2012). GoodmanKruskalGamma. Wolfram Language function.  [Link](https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/GoodmanKruskalGamma.html)
1. Goodman and Kruskal&apos;s gamma. (2022, Nov 23). In _Wikipedia_. [Link](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodman_and_Kruskal%27s_gamma]</kb-article>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/GoodmanKruskalGamma.html"/>
