    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#LocalAreaNetwork">
        <definition>A local area network (LAN) is a computer network that interconnects computers within a limited area such as a residence, school, laboratory, university campus or office building and has its network equipment and interconnects locally managed. Ethernet and Wi-Fi are the two most common transmission technologies in use for local area networks. Historical technologies include ARCNET, Token ring, and AppleTalk.</definition>
