        <definition>A real-time operating system (RTOS) is an operating system (OS) for real-time computing applications that processes data and events that have critically defined time constraints.</definition>
        <synonym>RTOS</synonym>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://dbpedia.org/resource/Real-time_operating_system"/>
